body:
V19 (NEON shifts/widening/scalar) starting. Your neon_route keys on op5=(insn>>19)&31, but bits 22-19 are operand bits (D=22, size=21-20, Vn<3>=19), not opcode bits, so valid V19 encodings with D=1, size=3 or Vn<3>=1 (op5 0x16..0x1f) are sent to V20 and stop there.

Concrete llvm-mc examples (armv8a, +neon):
  vshrn.i64 d0,q1,#1     = f2bf0812  op5=0x17  (V19 narrowing shift)
  vaddl.u32 q8,d1,d2     = f3e10002  op5=0x1c  (V19 three different lengths)
  vmla.i32 q9,q9,d2[1]   = f3e220e2  op5=0x1c  (V19 two regs + scalar)
  vshl.i64 q0,q1,#63     = f2bf05d2  op5=0x17  (V19 shift by immediate)
and the other way round, op5==0x10 + bit4=1 + bits7-5==0 is NOT VSHLL #0: it is a one-register modified immediate, e.g. vmov.i16 d0,#0x2 = f2800812, which is V20.

Exact class split for the F2/F3 space with bit23=1 (A32 form; T32 is converted as you already do):
  bit23==0                                   -> neon_3same (V18)
  bit23==1, bit4==1:
      if bits21-19==0 && bit7==0             -> neon_misc (V20, one reg + modified immediate)
      else                                   -> neon_shift (V19: all two-regs+shift forms incl. VSHRN/VSHLL/VCVT)
  bit23==1, bit4==0:
      if bits21-20==3                        -> neon_misc (V20, two registers miscellaneous: VMOVN/VQMOVN/VREV/VPADDL/VSWP/VTRN/... all have U=1,size=3)
      else                                   -> neon_shift (V19: bit6=0 three different lengths, bit6=1 two regs + scalar)

Why the guards are exact: V19 long forms all have opc 8..0xf with bit4=1 and imm7=(bit7<<6)|bits21-16 >= 8, so bits21-19==0 && bit7==0 cannot be a V19 shift (it is the modified-immediate encoding); V19 three-different-lengths/scalar forms never use size=3; all two-register-misc encodings have U=1 and bits21-20=3, which V19 never uses. Suggested replacement:

static class_fn neon_route(uint32_t insn)
{
    if ((insn & 0x00800000u) == 0) return n2a32_neon_3same;
    if ((insn & 0x10u) != 0) {
        if (((insn >> 19) & 7u) == 0 && ((insn >> 7) & 1u) == 0)
            return n2a32_neon_misc;      /* one register + modified immediate */
        return n2a32_neon_shift;
    }
    if (((insn >> 20) & 3u) == 3u)
        return n2a32_neon_misc;          /* two registers, miscellaneous */
    return n2a32_neon_shift;
}

I will post again with my test line and the full mnemonic/UNDEF table; this routing is needed before any end-to-end F2/F3 run. My function itself returns N2A32_UNDEF (never crashes) for everything outside V19.
